{
  "duration": 70.059,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.099,
      "end": 1.459,
      "text": "So welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 2.079,
      "end": 3.199,
      "text": "It's time to solve"
    },
    {
      "start": 3.639,
      "end": 4.599,
      "text": "one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 5.059,
      "end": 5.859,
      "text": "Now in this problem,"
    },
    {
      "start": 6.46,
      "end": 7.019,
      "text": "we have a"
    },
    {
      "start": 7.46,
      "end": 8.5,
      "text": "20-meter tower."
    },
    {
      "start": 9.059,
      "end": 10.099,
      "text": "From a point on the ground,"
    },
    {
      "start": 10.519,
      "end": 13.199,
      "text": "the angle of elevation to the top of the tower"
    },
    {
      "start": 13.779,
      "end": 15.46,
      "text": "is 45 degrees,"
    },
    {
      "start": 15.88,
      "end": 17.319,
      "text": "and we need to find the distance"
    },
    {
      "start": 17.84,
      "end": 19.139,
      "text": "from that point to the tower."
    },
    {
      "start": 19.699,
      "end": 20.399,
      "text": "Before solving,"
    },
    {
      "start": 20.899,
      "end": 24.219,
      "text": "let us quickly draw the right triangle in our mind."
    },
    {
      "start": 24.68,
      "end": 28.34,
      "text": "The height of the tower becomes the opposite side, which is"
    },
    {
      "start": 28.659,
      "end": 29.319,
      "text": "20 meters."
    },
    {
      "start": 29.84,
      "end": 34.439,
      "text": "The distance from the person to the tower becomes the adjacent side."
    },
    {
      "start": 34.84,
      "end": 35.419,
      "text": "Let us call it"
    },
    {
      "start": 35.759,
      "end": 35.879,
      "text": "X."
    },
    {
      "start": 36.559,
      "end": 45.099,
      "text": "Now, which trigonometric ratio connects the opposite side and the adjacent side? It is 10, because 10 theta equals opposite by adjacent."
    },
    {
      "start": 45.419,
      "end": 51.079,
      "text": "So we can write 1045 degrees equals 20 over X. Now, this is where the question becomes easy."
    },
    {
      "start": 51.559,
      "end": 53.199,
      "text": "We already know one standard value,"
    },
    {
      "start": 53.68,
      "end": 57.699,
      "text": "1045 degrees equals one, so one equals 20 divided by"
    },
    {
      "start": 58.0,
      "end": 58.119,
      "text": "X."
    },
    {
      "start": 58.439,
      "end": 59.499,
      "text": "Now cross-multiply,"
    },
    {
      "start": 59.84,
      "end": 61.939,
      "text": "we get X equals 20."
    },
    {
      "start": 62.639,
      "end": 65.699,
      "text": "So the distance from the point to the tower is 20 meters."
    },
    {
      "start": 66.139,
      "end": 66.479,
      "text": "Hence,"
    },
    {
      "start": 66.839,
      "end": 68.879,
      "text": "the correct answer is option D,"
    },
    {
      "start": 69.559,
      "end": 70.059,
      "text": "20 meters"
    }
  ],
